  "notes": "0 married filing separately, or head of household with a qualifying child counted for the credit; 1 single, qualifying surviving spouse, or head of household with no counted qualifying child; 2 married filing jointly. v2: a head of household with no counted qualifying child takes Step 4 like a single filer, and tax.us.2025.rule.eic-answer.not-married asks whether the filer was married at the end of 2025 (Step 4 question 1 stops only a married taxpayer filing as head of household). A head of household with a counted child stays 0, so the separated-spouse answer (Step 3 questions 3-5) is asked exactly as in v1. Every other status publishes v1's class and reads nothing new."
